WEBVTT

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:31.890
You...

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.150
broke your promise, didn't you?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.000
Thank goodness!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.260
You're awake!

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.030
It's all right.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.290
They're gone now.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.010
It's not cut, is it?

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.870
Back then...

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.030
It seemed like a fragment of a memory.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.250
I don't remember.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.430
Did those girls do that to you before?

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.830
But cutting a girl's hair is criminal! Criminal, I say!

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.230
But...

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.130
Before I lost my memories, and even now,

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.860
it seems inevitable that they'll cut my hair.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.740
I...

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.200
It's more than petty hatred. I feel like I'm despised.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.080
I could definitely feel their animosity.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.370
They said "promise," right?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.030
Is that...

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.480
It seems that before you lost your memories,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.000
you must've made a promise with those girls,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.170
and since you lost your memories, you ended up breaking that promise?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.140
I doubt they'll tell us the whole story, even if we ask them.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:35.430
They might even take advantage of your memory loss and lie to you.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.040
As such, I must still recommend that you keep your memory loss a secret.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.990
The people you work with don't seem like bad people,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.160
but we don't even know what your oldest friends, Toma and Shin, are like.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.210
And now that someone harbors animosity toward you,

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.790
there's no telling how information might leak out.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.720
I know.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.000
I don't know what promise I made to those girls,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.170
but I broke that promise.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.800
Because of that, I hurt someone or made them sad...

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:23.000
Are you all better now?

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.740
Yeah. Sorry for making you worry.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.860
I'm not totally up to speed yet, but...

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.210
It's okay. We'll help you out.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.100
Sawa, you're so reliable!

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.050
No, Mine, you're helping out, too.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.440
I think we can trust them.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.350
Hey...

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.670
There's something different about you.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.480
Ah!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.050
You think so?

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.640
I thought everything was going well, but I spoke too soon!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.090
If you asked me what it was, I couldn't tell you,

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.310
but something feels different.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:59.550
She's been spacing out a lot lately, but then again, she's always been like that.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.690
Great cover!

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.650
That's right...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.600
Today we're meeting about the trip.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.170
Trip?

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.110
You're not supposed to go too, are you?

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.960
Is everyone supposed to be at the meeting?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.620
What are you talking about?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.500
It's our orientation trip for part-timers,

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.480
so we talked about how we should all meet to discuss it.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.100
I meant, do you think everyone can come?

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.210
Of course.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.630
At first Shin said he couldn't make it because he was studying for exams, but...

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.640
Taking occasional breaks may improve the efficacy of your exam studying.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.510
So Shin said he'd come after all.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:40.060
So in the end, we can all go. Don't you remember?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.200
Yeah, I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.400
Hey, you don't look it at all.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.330
That's not true...

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.630
Three days and two nights on an island trip.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:58.380
Is it all right for me to go in my current state?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.000
This first hurdle is set too high, right?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.600
It'll be challenging to not make any mistakes during the trip.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.240
That said, it could also be a chance at getting your memories back,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.700
so we should think optimistically.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:12.680
Yeah.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:13.510
You.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:14.720
Yes?

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:18.180
What have you been mumbling to yourself over there?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.680
Take this to table three.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.560
A birthday cake?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.690
I haven't seen one of those in a while.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:38.470
Happy birthday to you. Happy birthday to you...

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:41.300
Happy birthday, dear...

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:46.830
I killed...

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.010
I...

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:53.440
...killed a man.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.220
What was that? That was Shin, wasn't it?

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.120
Was that another memory?

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.460
<i>Killed?</i>

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.470
What's wrong?

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.940
Nothing.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.670
It's nothing.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.010
I hope it won't rain.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:19.640
Huh?

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.130
Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:25.140
There'd be no point, if it rained and you couldn't see it.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.040
Couldn't see what?

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:32.080
What do you mean, "see what?" It was <i>your</i> idea.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.940
Mine?

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.050
This isn't good!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.900
Shin's looking right at you, too!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:42.520
It was you who said you wanted to see the Mnemid meteor shower.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.520
Just go along with it!

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:48.710
Ah, that's right.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.770
What else could it be?

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.850
I forgot.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.240
You're forgetting too much!

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:59.820
According to the weekly weather report, it should be mostly clear.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.310
I'm sure it'll be pretty.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.890
I'm looking forward to the meteor shower.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.320
<i>I said I wanted to see it...</i>

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.460
Hey.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.610
Are you all right with your studying?

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.650
I'm going because it's all right.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.120
True enough.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.710
By the way, Kento, you're a graduate student in math, right?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.470
Why don't you have him teach you?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.680
I don't mind, but organize your questions beforehand.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.750
That way, I won't waste my time on meaningless problems.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.230
We're all here.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:40.020
Now, I'd like to begin our meeting concerning the island trip this weekend, August 8th.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.350
To strengthen inter-staff relations at Meido no Hitsuji,

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:47.610
I planned on bringing us together under one roof.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.960
But, well, let's leave out the serious talk.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.780
Everyone, please enjoy yourselves.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.440
Looks like we made it out okay.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.910
But there's so much I don't know.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.250
It might be inevitable that everyone thinks I'm acting weird.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.500
At the moment, Mine and Shin are particularly dangerous.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:10.980
They look like they suspect something.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:18.440
Oh yeah, it might be a good idea to ask more questions that could give us hints about your memories.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.520
That's right.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:24.010
It would be nice if I could.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:29.410
I'm sorry. I said I'd do my best, but it's not enough, is it?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.310
That's not true.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:35.750
It's a huge help having you here.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.060
I'm glad you think so.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.510
But we can't seem to recover any helpful memories.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.510
That's true.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:48.560
Watch out!

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.400
The light's red.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.400
I'm sorry!

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.910
It's dangerous to space out like that.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.030
This has happened before, too.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.910
You don't remember me, do you?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.480
Of course not.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.540
Goodbye, then.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.940
Have you met him before?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:25.160
Just now, I felt something flutter in my chest.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.310
Me too.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.710
Wow!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.320
What a beautiful view!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.710
Plus, this is my first time riding in one of these!

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.290
Ah, we're here!

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.480
What a nice place.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.090
Yeah.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:34.510
Hey, Shin's looking over at you again.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.130
I wonder why. It looks like there's something he really wants to say.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.270
Do you think he knows that you lost your memory?

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:59.440
Wasn't it supposed to be clear this weekend with 0% chance of rain, Ken?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.030
That was the forecast during the week,

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.860
but the weather changes rapidly.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:05.810
What can you do?

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.830
What a downpour!

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:11.840
Now, everyone. I think this rain will end soon.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.910
I don't see any sign of that. How do you figure?

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.490
I can tell by the smell.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:19.420
I see.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.230
Smell, huh?

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:24.130
Can you really predict the weather by smell?

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.630
It doesn't look like it's going to stop.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:43.720
You told me to promise you just one thing.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.830
<i>Kento?</i>

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.280
I wonder what the promise was.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.020
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.250
It stopped raining.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.510
Wow, Waka was right! The rain really stopped!

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.840
It stopped just like he said it would.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.390
That's kind of amazing.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.380
It is.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.140
What kind of smell does rain have?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.300
<i>Was that...</i>

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.330
What is it? Is there something on my face?

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.270
Oh, no. It's nothing.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.310
You look like you've been daydreaming.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.800
<i>How can he tell?</i>

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.150
Hey, let's ask him about the vision you saw.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:40.050
Um, as I was listening to the rain, I remembered the festival we went to before.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:44.170
There were lots of pretty wind chimes in the merchant stalls,

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:49.390
and while it drizzled, you let me under your umbrella.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.180
He's so inexpressive again!

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.080
You remember, don't you?

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.520
We were at a festival?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.740
Hey!

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.190
We're over here!

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:07.280
From the looks of it, Kento doesn't know what you're talking about.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:14.740
But all the visions you've seen up until now have been too disjointed, and there isn't anything connecting them.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:16.600
The people in them are always different, too.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.320
I wonder what's going on.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.700
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.500
<i>I wonder if they're experiences I had before I lost my memories.</i>

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:28.340
Now then!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.670
While we wait for the meteor shower, let's play a game!

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.840
Team air hockey, go!

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.840
The first contenders are...

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:38.350
Shin and Toma

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.730
versus Kento and Ikki!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.470
Shin, you're on offense, I'm on defense.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:48.700
Is that all right?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.780
Of course. There isn't any other formation.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:52.810
Hm...

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:56.200
Looks like <i>some</i> people are blurting out their strategy.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.990
I wonder if they're underestimating us.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:02.810
Of course not. You're good at this kind of game, aren't you, Ikki?

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.590
You're in the table tennis club, right?

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:07.860
Wrong. I'm in the darts circle now.

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:11.910
I'm good at almost any game that uses my hands.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.850
That's pretty much all games.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:16.510
You don't need a strategy meeting?

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.530
It's already decided.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:21.810
I'll come up with the plan, and Ikkyu will do the fighting.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:22.900
Hey, Ken.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.520
Ikkyu? He means Ikki, right?

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.470
You don't have to be polite and reveal our strategy, too.

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:27.420
Now it's fair. We'll just show them that they'll still lose.
Is that a nickname?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.460
His real name?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.770
Either way, it doesn't suit him at all!

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:31.320
Now it's fair. We'll just show them that they'll still lose.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.470
I'm the one who has to do the work.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.320
Not that I mind.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.780
They sure talk big.

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:40.530
Well, we don't plan on losing either.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:45.540
Okay, it looks like both teams are ready, so let the game begin!

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:57.880
All right!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.760
Show them a false opening.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.810
Kento and Ikki win!

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:09.380
Ikki is seriously just too good.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:13.740
No, Kento's flawless strategies are really something, too.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.360
Damn... I don't think I can win in a game that uses hands.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.500
I know, cards.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:19.910
Let's play poker.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.080
Fine with me.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:26.340
But like I said before, I'm good at any game that uses my hands.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.260
Huh?

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:31.210
Well, poker uses hands in a different sense.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm seriously starting to think there's no winning against Ikki.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.590
Sorry about that.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.470
I'm glad we came after all.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:43.950
That's true. Thank you, Orion.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.340
But I haven't done anything.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.720
I'm sure I couldn't've done this alone.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:52.500
Just having you here is a huge help.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.300
I see. I'm glad.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.360
You know, I'm happy that I'm with you, too.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:02.370
I know getting your memories back is the top priority,

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:07.240
but I'm happy I get to experience all these new things with you.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:08.890
<i>Orion.</i>

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:10.620
Hey.

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.180
It's our turn next.

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:14.500
Oh, right.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:19.310
Let's beat the crap out of Waka and Mine!

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.640
Okay?

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.640
The Mnemid meteor shower.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:41.740
It is said that those who see it will etch wonderful memories into their hearts.

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:46.140
I hope that tonight will be a wonderful memory.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:48.610
Mr. Manager, how much further?

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:49.730
Just a little further.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:52.420
You said that before.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.920
This time I mean it.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:56.420
This is pretty tough.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.980
Are you okay?

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.090
Yeah.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:03.110
You tried hard at air hockey, so maybe you've used up all your strength.

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.740
But good job beating the manager!

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.800
Yeah. I surprised myself.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:10.560
The manager's puck disappeared for a second, too!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.560
You did well to hit it back.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:14.310
I had my eyes closed the whole time.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:17.370
What? So you hit that by chance?

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.190
Well, it was fun either wa—

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:20.600
Huh?

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.820
Shin.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.320
You're exhausted, aren't you?

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.850
Not... at all.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:30.330
Here.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.400
Give me your hand.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.420
Come on, just give it.

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.800
I'm fine by myself.

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:43.470
You know,

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.470
there's something I want to ask you.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.800
I think being alone with him is a bad idea right now!

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.440
We don't know what he's going to ask.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.740
You have to make up an excuse!

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:58.430
Um... We should catch up to the others,

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.400
or they'll worry.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.500
That was dangerous.

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:09.660
I'm okay.

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:12.500
I'm fine. So...

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.320
<i>I killed...</i>

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.480
<i>I...</i>

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:18.790
<i>...killed a man.</i>

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:23.670
Not that way!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.490
Now I have no choice.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.430
I guess I should take this to them.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:37.520
No...

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.590
It's no use.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:44.650
Because this is where he...

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:33.830
I'm coming in.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:36.720
Hey.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.870
How long are you going to sleep for?

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:41.390
Shin?

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.160
It's already ten.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:47.380
Huh?

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.770
August 1st?

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.390
You're half asleep, aren't you?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.270
Seriously.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.770
What are you spacing out for?

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.350
Let me snap you out of it.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:45.630
What is it?

00:22:47.110 --> 00:22:49.290
Aren't you going to freak out in embarrassment today?

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:53.170
You are <i>really</i> out of it.

00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:58.930
I'll sign the forms to get you discharged, so get dressed by then.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:01.750
When I get back, I'll come in without saying anything.

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:02.610
Um...

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:06.830
Discharge? What is he talking about?

00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:10.150
Orion, I think I...

00:23:14.170 --> 00:23:14.820
Orion?

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:20.680
Hey,

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:22.950
what's going on,

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:24.960
Orion?

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:27.980
Do you know the trick to winning in air hockey?

00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:30.020
To maintain a strong defense, no matter what.

00:23:30.020 --> 00:23:32.150
You can't let your opponent score a single point.

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:33.940
The best offense is a strong defense.

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:35.780
Or is it the other way around?

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:39.430
Also, boys shouldn't ride in swan boats together.
